-- D (2026-10-15): researched Qatari investors and ADR-001 evidence axes for the
-- prepared public profiles (fix-forward of 20261222110000).
--
-- 1. Facts are stored on ADR-001's evidence axis, conservatively: a
--    statement found on a read public page DOCUMENT_SUPPORTED (or
--    MULTI_SOURCE_SUPPORTED), a reported one SELF_REPORTED, an unread one
--    NO_EVIDENCE; never "VERIFIED" (Capital Q verified nothing). Each
--    source keeps its own reading status. The Qatar five carry no quotes (owner direction 2026-10-15: no quotes,
--    mandates, decisions or endorsements attributed to a real person or
--    organisation). Each fact's truth_class / evidence_status /
--    lifecycle_status, retrieval date and uncertainty label go in
--    profile.evidenceAxes; Muhannad Taslaq gains one re-read Alchemist Doha
--    fact. Nothing about them is duplicated.
-- 2. Four further researched, UNCLAIMED public profiles: Qatar Development
--    Bank, QIA Fund of Funds Program, Rasmal Ventures, Doha Tech Angels.
-- 3. QDB, Rasmal Ventures and Doha Tech Angels invest in companies, so each
--    becomes a canonical, unclaimed investor organisation in the platform
--    tenant of 20261222100000, exactly as QInvest/AlRayan/Alchemist did: no
--    login, membership, representative or mandate, verification
--    'unverified', inbound and deployment unknown (NULL). QIA's programme
--    invests in funds, not companies, so it stays a research profile only.
--
-- Additive and idempotent: upserts by key, nothing deleted. The JSON
-- document is exactly `toPreparedUpsert` (plus the derived id) for
-- scripts/seed/research/qatar-five.v1.json then qatar-investors.v1.json
-- (apps/q-api test `prepared-follow-up.test.ts` fails if they drift).

